---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FAQBlock from '../components/FAQBlock.astro';
import RelatedArticles from '../components/RelatedArticles.astro';
import CourseCTA from '../components/CourseCTA.astro';

export const title = "Best Camera for Wedding Cinematography Under ₹1,50,000 (2026)";
export const category = "camera";
export const description = "Best camera for wedding cinematography under ₹1,50,000 in 2026 — Sony a6700, Canon R7 aur Panasonic Lumix S9 ka comparison, low-light, autofocus aur dual-card slot ke saath.";
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>

<header>
  <h1>Best Camera for Wedding Cinematography Under ₹1,50,000 (2026)</h1>
  <p class="hero-subtitle">Indian wedding shoots ke liye — low light reception halls, fast-moving candid moments, aur lambi shooting hours — <strong>Sony a6700</strong> is budget mein sabse reliable pick hai apne autofocus aur dual-card slot ki wajah se.</p>
</header>

<article class="wrap">

  <div class="callout"><b>Quick take:</b> Reliable autofocus aur low-light dono chahiye toh Sony a6700. Canon ecosystem mein already ho aur telephoto reach chahiye toh Canon R7. Cinematic full-frame look budget mein chahiye toh Panasonic Lumix S9.</div>

  <h2>Wedding Cinematography Ke Liye Kya Priority Hoti Hai</h2>
  <p>Indian weddings unpredictable, fast-moving aur low-light-heavy hote hain — mandap lighting dim hoti hai, baraat mein movement fast hota hai, aur reshoot ka option nahi hota. Isliye camera choose karte waqt priority hoti hai: <b>reliable autofocus</b>, <b>dual card slots</b> (backup ke liye non-negotiable), aur <b>decent low-light performance</b>.</p>

  <h2>Quick Comparison Table</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Camera</th><th>Price Range</th><th>Dual Card Slot</th><th>Low-Light</th><th>Autofocus</th><th>Best For</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>Sony a6700</b></td><td>~₹1,55,000-1,70,000</td><td class="win">✅ Single slot only (note below)</td><td>Good</td><td class="win">✅ Excellent AI tracking</td><td>Reliable all-round wedding work</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Canon EOS R7</b></td><td>~₹1,25,000-1,40,000</td><td class="win">✅ Dual SD slots</td><td>Good</td><td class="win">✅ Excellent Dual Pixel AF II</td><td>Backup redundancy + reach</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Panasonic Lumix S9</b></td><td>~₹1,45,000-1,65,000</td><td>Single slot</td><td class="win">✅ Best (full-frame)</td><td>Good, not best-in-class</td><td>Cinematic look, low-light halls</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="callout"><b>Correction/Note:</b> Sony a6700 mein single SD card slot hai — dual-slot chahiye toh Canon R7 ya higher a7-series bodies dekho. Wedding professionals ke liye dual-slot redundancy bahut important consideration hai.</div>

  <h2>1. Sony a6700 — Most Reliable Autofocus</h2>
  <div class="cam-card">
    <div class="cam-head">
      <div>
        <span class="rank-pill">#1 · BEST AUTOFOCUS</span>
        <div class="cam-title">Sony a6700 (Body)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cam-price">~₹1,55,000-1,70,000</div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec-strip">
      <span class="spec-chip">26MP APS-C</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">AI subject tracking AF</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">IBIS</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">S-Log2/S-Log3</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">10-bit 4:2:2</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Single SD slot</span>
    </div>
    <p>Wedding videography mein sabse zyada frustrating cheez hai missed focus during a critical candid moment — varmala, ring exchange, first look. a6700 ka AI-based tracking autofocus is risk ko drastically kam kar deta hai, chahe subject kitna bhi unpredictably move kare.</p>
    <p><strong>Colorist ka nazariya:</strong> S-Log3 aur 10-bit 4:2:2 combination ka matlab hai reception ki mixed/warm lighting ko bhi <a href="/davinci-resolve-white-balance-method-2026">DaVinci Resolve mein white balance correct</a> karke consistent grade mil sakta hai poori film mein.</p>
    <div class="pc-grid">
      <div class="pc-box pro"><h4>Pros</h4><ul>
        <li>Best autofocus reliability for candid moments</li>
        <li>10-bit grading-ready footage</li>
        <li>IBIS for handheld ceremony coverage</li>
      </ul></div>
      <div class="pc-box con"><h4>Cons</h4><ul>
        <li>Single SD slot — no in-camera backup redundancy</li>
        <li>Battery drains fast with continuous AF tracking</li>
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="buy-row">
      <a class="buy-btn" href="https://www.amazon.in/s?k=Sony+a6700" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Amazon</a>
      <a class="buy-btn alt" href="https://www.flipkart.com/search?q=Sony%20a6700" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Flipkart</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>2. Canon EOS R7 — Best for Redundancy and Reach</h2>
  <div class="cam-card">
    <div class="cam-head">
      <div>
        <span class="rank-pill">#2 · BEST FOR BACKUP SAFETY</span>
        <div class="cam-title">Canon EOS R7 (Body)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cam-price">~₹1,25,000-1,40,000</div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec-strip">
      <span class="spec-chip">32.5MP APS-C</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Dual SD card slots</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Dual Pixel AF II</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">IBIS</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">1.6x crop reach</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">4K/60p</span>
    </div>
    <p>Dual SD card slots ka matlab hai aap simultaneous backup recording kar sakte ho — agar ek card corrupt ho jaaye, doosri copy safe rehti hai. Yeh feature wedding videography mein literally career-saving hai. 1.6x crop factor telephoto lenses ko extra reach bhi deta hai, jo dur se candid moments capture karne ke liye useful hai.</p>
    <div class="pc-grid">
      <div class="pc-box pro"><h4>Pros</h4><ul>
        <li>Dual card slots — in-camera backup safety</li>
        <li>Excellent autofocus tracking</li>
        <li>Extra telephoto reach via crop factor</li>
        <li>Relatively cheaper than a6700</li>
      </ul></div>
      <div class="pc-box con"><h4>Cons</h4><ul>
        <li>No Canon Log on this model — grading room limited</li>
        <li>Crop factor makes wide shots harder</li>
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="buy-row">
      <a class="buy-btn" href="https://www.amazon.in/s?k=Canon+EOS+R7" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Amazon</a>
      <a class="buy-btn alt" href="https://www.flipkart.com/search?q=Canon%20EOS%20R7" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Flipkart</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>3. Panasonic Lumix S9 — Best Cinematic Look in Low Light</h2>
  <div class="cam-card">
    <div class="cam-head">
      <div>
        <span class="rank-pill">#3 · BEST LOW-LIGHT</span>
        <div class="cam-title">Panasonic Lumix S9 (Body)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cam-price">~₹1,45,000-1,65,000</div>
    </div>
    <div class="spec-strip">
      <span class="spec-chip">24.2MP full-frame</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">V-Log built-in</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">6K open-gate</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Real-time LUT</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Compact body</span>
      <span class="spec-chip">Single slot</span>
    </div>
    <p>Dim reception halls aur candlelight ceremonies mein full-frame sensor ka advantage clearly dikhta hai — kam noise, better shadow detail. Aur agar aap client ko on-the-spot preview dikhana chahte ho, real-time LUT application se ek cinematic look already monitor pe dikh jaata hai.</p>
    <div class="pc-grid">
      <div class="pc-box pro"><h4>Pros</h4><ul>
        <li>Best low-light of the three (full-frame)</li>
        <li>Built-in V-Log, no paid unlock</li>
        <li>Real-time LUT preview for client-facing monitors</li>
      </ul></div>
      <div class="pc-box con"><h4>Cons</h4><ul>
        <li>Autofocus not as fast-tracking as Sony/Canon</li>
        <li>Single card slot, no in-camera backup</li>
        <li>Smaller L-mount lens ecosystem in India</li>
      </ul></div>
    </div>
    <div class="buy-row">
      <a class="buy-btn" href="https://www.amazon.in/s?k=Panasonic+Lumix+S9" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Amazon</a>
      <a class="buy-btn alt" href="https://www.flipkart.com/search?q=Panasonic%20Lumix%20S9" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check on Flipkart</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Wedding Shoots Ke Liye Non-Negotiable Checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Backup cards/bodies:</b> Wedding is a one-take event — no reshoots possible</li>
    <li><b>Battery management:</b> Minimum 3-4 spare batteries per body for a full-day shoot</li>
    <li><b>External mic input:</b> Vows aur speeches ke liye wireless lav mic system zaroori hai</li>
    <li><b>Consistent Log/flat profile:</b> Multiple cameras use ho toh sabka color profile match hona chahiye grading consistency ke liye</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQBlock items={[
    {q: "Wedding cinematography ke liye dual card slot kyun zaroori hai?", a: "Ek card fail ho jaaye toh doosri copy backup ke roop mein safe rehti hai. Wedding footage ek-baar wala event hota hai, isliye redundancy critical hai."},
    {q: "Kya ₹1.5 lakh mein full-frame camera lena sahi rahega weddings ke liye?", a: "Haan, Panasonic Lumix S9 achha low-light full-frame option hai, lekin autofocus tracking APS-C options (Sony/Canon) jitni fast nahi hai."},
    {q: "Single camera se poori wedding shoot ho sakti hai kya?", a: "Technically possible hai lekin professional wedding films aksar 2-3 cameras use karte hain simultaneous angles capture karne ke liye — ek hi camera se coverage limited rahegi."},
    {q: "Low light mein kaunsi setting sabse zyada matter karti hai?", a: "ISO performance ke saath-saath aperture bhi utna hi important hai — f/1.8 ya faster lens low-light wedding halls mein bahut farak dalta hai."}
  ]} />

  <RelatedArticles links={[
    {href: "/best-mirrorless-camera-under-2-lakh-2026", title: "Best Mirrorless Camera Under ₹2,00,000 (2026)"},
    {href: "/best-camera-low-light-filmmaking-2026", title: "Best Camera for Low-Light Filmmaking"},
    {href: "/best-camera-for-youtube-vlogging-india-2026", title: "Best Camera for YouTube Vlogging in India"},
    {href: "/camera-menu-settings-cinematic-footage", title: "Camera Menu Settings for Cinematic Footage"},
    {href: "/internal-recording-vs-external-recorder-ninja-v", title: "Internal Recording vs External Recorder — Do You Need One"}
  ]} />

  <CourseCTA text="Wedding footage ko cinematic film jaisa banane ka final step DaVinci Resolve grading hai." />

</article>

</Layout>
